#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""San Juan Hill: Santiago de Cuba, 1 July 1898.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Shafter's V Corps comes out of the jungle on the road to Santiago and
must cross the San Juan River under the fire of Spanish Mausers before
it can climb Kettle Hill and the San Juan Heights.  On the right are
the dismounted troopers of the Cavalry Division, among them the 1st US
Volunteer Cavalry, the Rough Riders, and Lieutenant Colonel Theodore
Roosevelt on his horse Little Texas.  Play either side against the
computer, or against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./sanjuan (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.sanjuan.json.  ./sanjuan --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

